OL,3,GNEWSAOrienteering course getting
OL,4,Avillage moving
OL,5,
OL,6,FA public orienteering course is helping
OL,7,Fvillagers get more active.
OL,9,FOrienteering involves navigating
OL,10,Fbetween checkpoints using a special map
OL,11,Fbut without a set route, and the course
OL,12,Fin Flimby, Maryport, was developed with
OL,13,Fthe help of pupils from Flimby Primary
OL,14,FSchool.
OL,16,FThey helped to design the course to
OL,17,Finclude elements from their curriculum
OL,18,Fand head Tanya Peers said seeing the
OL,19,Fchildren's ideas come to life felt
OL,20,F"really special".
